## Context
Author clarification, 2026-11-07: locate where implementation-language choices happen (Imagine, Plan, or elsewhere), and inspect history for concrete poor choices IDH could redress. Do not impose a predetermined Bash/Python/Rust rule.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Harness-doctor retains an on-demand diagnostic locating actual language-choice decision points and reconstructing bounded historical cases with source evidence.
- [ ] Controls distinguish a failure mechanism a different language can remove from a logic error that survives translation; reproduce a specific mechanism when surviving inputs permit it.
- [ ] Recommend or apply a targeted correction only when evidence supports it; unverified incidents and no actionable correction remain explicit valid outcomes.
- [ ] No blanket language rule, speculative rewrite, routine healthcheck, scheduled sweep, or merge-gate integration.
